  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Main article",
      "text": "As of now, standards can be searched on the new platform norml , which offers numerous improvements, such as the full-text search. Access to the previous platform is still available until 31 March 2023.\n\nIn addition to the existing standards from ASTM International, DIN (DE), Electrosuisse (DE), IEEE International, INB / SM / ES / SIA National / SIA International (DE/FR), ISO (EN), and VDI (DE), the IEC standards are now also available.\n\nThe IEC is an international standards organization in the fields of electrical engineering, electronics and information technology. It unites more than 170 countries worldwide and offers a global, neutral and independent standardisation platform. IEC standards serve as the basis for risk and quality management and are used in certifications to check whether manufacturers’ promises are fulfilled.\n\nFor licensing reasons, the standards portal normI is available to members of ETH Zurich only.\n\n#KnowMore – The prepared content issued by the ETH Library is at your free disposal and gives you a head start.\n\nMore than just data – Benefit from know-how"
    }
  ],
